WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.260
Marjorie was likely
bitten by a tiger shark,

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.473
one of the main culprits
of shark attacks

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.907
on surfers in Hawaii.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.517
Tiger sharks tend to
be solitary hunters.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.886
They're feeding on
large prey items

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:23.289
and they have the jaws and
the hardware that enable them

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.025
to take those big prey items.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.695
But they're also not picky--
they'll eat whatever they can.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.000
Known as the "garbage
can of the ocean,"

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:40.140
the tiger shark has the hardware
to chew up anything it finds--

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.142
even license plates
and old tires.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.949
So here you have a site of
jaws from about a 12-foot tiger

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:53.353
shark, and you can see the
numbers of teeth that are

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.288
here and the size of the teeth.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:58.391
They're big, they're heavily
serrated-- even the serrations

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.793
have serrations on them.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.896
As that jaw's moving,
it's slicing across,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.099
and these become little
blades like on a chainsaw.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.534
Not only do they
have lots of teeth,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.769
they have lots of
replacement teeth behind,

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:13.406
so they always have a full
set of teeth rolling in.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.276
When they encounter
soft, squishy humans,

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.812
easily able to get
severely damaged

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.313
by such strong, powerful jaws.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.822
On Marjorie's sunset
surf, time and location

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.924
worked against her.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:36.196
Tiger sharks are
nocturnal hunters,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:42.635
and she was surfing in an
area inhabited by sea turtles.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:46.206
So a shark swimming along
toward dusk or at night,

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.408
it sees something
vaguely on the surface,

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:52.078
it's going to come up
and investigate it.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.447
You're sitting on this
board with your arms

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.716
off to the side, which
look like little flippers,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.720
and a shark coming up from
below might mistake this person

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.922
on a board for a turtle
that's flapping around

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.125
and give you an
investigatory bite.

